E TRANSLATED AND MUST NOT BE DROPPED -- OpenAI has nowhere to put the flag, so it becomes PLAIN TEXT in front of the content; dropping it would teach the model that an outage and an absence are the same thing, which here is the difference between "the house does not own it" and a wrong answer. ELIGIBILITY IS AN EXPLICIT ALLOWLIST, NOT AN INFERENCE: GROQ_READ_ONLY_TOOL_NAMES beside the tool definitions in gabi-tools.ts, 13 read-only names, every one mutates:false. A loop rides Groq only if EVERY tool it offers is on it; one unlisted name and the WHOLE LOOP stays 100% Anthropic. It is a LITERAL and deliberately NOT a spread of the family arrays -- the spread reads better and is wrong, because it makes a tool added tomorrow eligible BY DEFAULT as a side effect of a commit about something else. WHY PER LOOP AND NOT PER TURN: a loop carrying a mutating tool also carries the state that decides whether to call it, so letting its "safe" turns ride Groq would put the cheap model in the seat that PROPOSES the write. Nothing from GABI_DELEGATED_VERB_NAMES or GABI_CONFIRM_VERB_NAMES can be on it, asserted. SHADOW IS EXCLUDED AND IT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT: shadowing a tool loop would run the loop twice and EXECUTE EVERY TOOL TWICE with it, against live estate services. So tool loops go straight to first-with-fallback under the existing GABI_GROQ var -- no new env var, nothing new for the owner to set. PER-TURN FALLBACK THEN STICKY: an error, timeout, empty 200, a tool this turn did not offer, or arguments that fail validation replays THAT pass on the pinned Haiku from identical state -- safe precisely because the failed pass's tools were never executed. Once a loop has fallen back it FINISHES on Haiku; ping-ponging mid-loop would leave a conversation half-translated and half-native, two grammars to be wrong about instead of one. ARGUMENT VALIDATION IS NEW and is the reason a translation layer is allowed to exist: the Anthropic path never needed it because the model emitting the call and the schema constraining it are one vendor’s. A different vendor’s open-weights model is exactly where a plausible call with a wrong-shaped argument is likely and nothing downstream would notice -- runTool would hand junk to a catalogue query and get an empty result, which READS AS "the house does not have it". Checked: required present, no undeclared property, declared scalar type, enum membership. A pass that produced CALLS is tool_use WHATEVER finish_reason claimed -- read finish_reason alone and a server saying "stop" beside a tool_calls array would have its calls dropped and its narration posted as the answer, the 2026-08-18 silent partial through a new door. PINS UNCHANGED from phase 1 (openai/gpt-oss-120b, max_tokens floored 512, reasoning_effort low, 4s ceiling, key on Authorization only), and both providers get the SAME system prompt byte for byte (asserted) -- a fork would make every comparison a comparison of two different questions. LOG LINE extended per the convention AND per the bug that bit phase 1 (the field-by-field logger silently drops unknown keys, which is how the first status fix shipped as a no-op): each new field went in BOTH the param type and the emitted object. outcome gains "ineligible" beside groq|fallback; every line carries "iteration" and "tools_offered"; an ineligible line carries "ineligible_reason" (tool_not_allowlisted|posture_shadow) and "blocked_tools". NO accountTurn on a Groq pass -- gabi_turn means ANTHROPIC spend and must keep meaning that. Never the reply TEXT, asserted with a sentinel. THE PHASE-1 GUARD WAS REPLACED, NOT DELETED: the build-failing test that kept a tool turn off api.groq.com in every posture is now a stricter set (shadowed and ineligible loops still make zero Groq requests; off is still byte-identical to before the rung existed; every failure class still falls through invisibly). NO MIGRATION (no D1 on this Worker). Tests before deploy: test/gabi-groq.test.ts 44 -> 82, workspace 2269 -> 2307 pass / 0 fail, typecheck clean; no existing assertion weakened. Deployed from a THROWAWAY WORKTREE of HEAD with the node_modules junction (docs/info/worktree-deploys.md); teardown in the mandated order, .bin 51 before / 51 after the rmdir of the link / 51 after git worktree remove. VERIFIED LIVE (GET https://discord.heygabi.ai/api/health, 200): gabi_groq_scope now toolless_calls_plus_read_only_tool_loops_first_only, gabi_groq_tool_allowlist lists the 13 names, feature gabi_groq_tool_loops present, and every pre-existing field unchanged -- gabi_groq first / ready true / model openai/gpt-oss-120b, gabi_edge full, gabi_tools 2, gabi_tool_max_iterations 3, mentions enabled, all 11 configured rows true. No secret-shaped value in the body. NOT VERIFIED: *** NO LIVE GROQ TOOL CALL HAS EVER BEEN MADE FROM THIS REPO *** -- every test drives an injected fetch. Whether Groq accepts this exact tools body, whether openai/gpt-oss-120b CALLS THESE TOOLS ACCURATELY (the real question, and the shadow ladder cannot answer it without executing tools twice, which is why there is no shadow step here), how often a loop falls back, and what the savings actually are, are all unknown until a real @mention exercises a tool loop. The posture is already "first", so the very next tool-bearing mention is that first live call.
